riscv: dts: sophgo: cv18xx: add SARADC, enable on the Duo family

Wire up the on-SoC 3-channel SARADC (Successive Approximation ADC) so the
in-tree IIO driver can bind. The driver (drivers/iio/adc/sophgo-cv1800b-adc.c,
compatible "sophgo,cv1800b-saradc") is already built in via
CONFIG_SOPHGO_CV1800B_ADC=y -- the only thing missing was a device-tree
node, so nothing probed and no /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device* appeared.

Add the controller to the shared cv18xx.dtsi, disabled by default. The
SARADC block is identical across the CV1800B, SG2002 and SG2000, so the
node lives in the common dtsi and each board just flips it on:

  reg        0x030f0000 / 0x1000        (top-domain SARADC)
  clocks     <&clk CLK_SARADC>
  interrupts 100 == SOC_PERIPHERAL_IRQ(84), IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH
             (raw number to match this tree's cv18xx.dtsi convention)

Values match the mainline node (arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x.dtsi in
newer kernels) and the binding example
(Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/sophgo,cv1800b-saradc.yaml).

Enable the node on all three boards -- Milk-V Duo (CV1800B), Duo 256M
(SG2002) and Duo S (SG2000) -- exposing in_voltage{0,1,2}_raw plus
in_voltage_scale (12-bit, 3.3 V reference).

No pin muxing is set here on purpose: the controller probes and all three
IIO channels become readable without it. A channel whose pad is not muxed
to the analog input simply reports a floating-input reading rather than a
meaningful voltage -- correct behaviour, just not useful until the pad is
routed. The per-board analog-input pad mux is left to a later, board-
specific change.

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv18xx.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv18xx.dtsi
@@ -477,6 +477,28 @@
 			#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 		};

+		saradc: adc@30f0000 {
+			compatible = "sophgo,cv1800b-saradc";
+			reg = <0x030f0000 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&clk CLK_SARADC>;
+			interrupts = <100 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+
+			channel@0 {
+				reg = <0>;
+			};
+
+			channel@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+			};
+
+			channel@2 {
+				reg = <2>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		plic: interrupt-controller@70000000 {
 			reg = <0x70000000 0x4000000>;
 			interrupts-extended = <&cpu0_intc 11>, <&cpu0_intc 9>;
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv1800b-milkv-duo.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv1800b-milkv-duo.dts
@@ -60,3 +60,7 @@
 &watchdog0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&saradc {
+	status = "okay";
+};
